# Terminal Execution Rules
- For any command expected to run longer than 15 seconds, you MUST prefix it with progress echoes.
- Example pattern: 
  echo ">>> [1/3] Installing dependencies..." && npm install && \
  echo ">>> [2/3] Building project..." && npm run build && \
  echo ">>> [3/3] Done."
- NEVER run silent long-running commands. Always provide intermediate stdout feedback.
- If a command requires interactive input, use non-interactive flags (-y, --yes, --non-interactive) or abort and ask me.